    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Over 20 hands, each player declares five contracts (two trump, three negative). In trump contracts each trick won scores +50; in negative contracts certain cards or tricks incur penalties. The player with the highest net score after all 20 hands wins.',
      'Turn-flow example: Must follow suit. In trump contracts, must trump if unable to follow (even underruff). In negative contracts, no trumps; if unable to follow, discard a penalty card if you have one. In Rıfkı and Kupa (Hearts), hearts may not be led unless already broken or you have only hearts. Penalty cards must be played when a higher card of the suit has been played to the trick.',
      'Scoring example: Trump contract: +50 per trick to winner (total +650). Negative contracts: Rıfkı (K♥) -320; Kız (Queens) -100 each; Erkek (Kings and Jacks) -60 each; Kupa (Hearts) -30 each; Son İki (last two tricks) -180 each; El Almaz (each trick) -50. Highest net after 20 rounds wins. Highest net points after 20 rounds..',
